V. 48. All men will believe-And receive him as the Messiah.  And this will give such umbrage to the Romans that they 

  will come and subvert both our place-Temple; 

  and nation-Both our Church and state.  Were they really afraid of this? Or was it a fair colour only?  Certainly it was no more.  For they could not but know, that he that raised the dead was able to conquer the Romans.
